---
// Cancellation and Refund Policy — final copy, Nov 2, 2026.
// Linked from the footer's Fine Print row, the enrollment emails, and Sawyer
// checkout, so the URL (/cancellation-policy) must not change. When the copy
// changes, update `updated` below in the same commit.
import PolicyPage from '@/layouts/PolicyPage.astro';
---

<PolicyPage
  title="Cancellation and Refund Policy | STAND"
  description="How deposits, tuition, cancellations, and refunds work for STAND cohorts."
  heading="Cancellation and Refund Policy"
  updated="2026-11-02"
>
  <h2>Deposit</h2>
  <p>
    The $100 deposit holds your child's seat in our cohort, goes toward tuition, and is
    non-refundable.
  </p>

  <h2>Before the cohort starts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The balance of tuition is charged 14 days before the first session.</li>
    <li>If you cancel more than 14 days before the first session, you won't be charged the balance.</li>
    <li>If you cancel within 14 days of the first session, the balance is non-refundable.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>After the cohort starts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Once the program begins, there are no refunds.</li>
    <li>Rather than cancel, you can move to a future STAND cohort if a seat is open.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Missed sessions</h2>
  <p>
    We don't refund, credit, or offer make-ups for missed sessions. When possible, we'll send a
    recap so your child can catch up.
  </p>

  <h2>If STAND cancels a session</h2>
  <p>We'll schedule a make-up session for your child. If we can't, we'll refund that session.</p>

  <h2>If STAND cancels the cohort before it starts</h2>
  <p>You'll get a full refund, including your deposit, or you can move to a future cohort.</p>

  <h2>How to cancel</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:hello@standkids.com">hello@standkids.com</a>. Cancellations count from
    the date we receive your email.
  </p>
</PolicyPage>
